# Cloudflare Pages joins a header with a comma when MORE THAN ONE rule matches the same file
# ("Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *" twice becomes "*, *"), and browsers reject that as invalid CORS.
# So every header below is set by exactly ONE rule. Do not repeat a header in a second block.
#
# Block 1 (every file): the cross-origin headers the sandbox iframe needs (it sends "Origin: null").
# Block 2 (versioned folder): caching only. Content-Type is left to Cloudflare, which already serves
# .js, .json, .wasm and .zip with the right types.

/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/v0.29.5/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
